%I A399766 #8 Sep 17 2026 23:59:48
%S A399766 1,0,0,0,0,2,0,2,0,32,0,44,0,32990,2594
%N A399766 Number of unlabeled directed strongly regular graphs on n vertices.
%C A399766 The parameters (v,k,t,lambda,mu) of a directed strongly regular graph have their usual meaning: v is the number of vertices, every vertex has in-degree and out-degree k, t is the number of undirected edges incident with each vertex, and the number of directed paths of length 2 from x to y is lambda if x is adjacent to y and mu otherwise.
%H A399766 A. E. Brouwer, <a href="https://homepages.cwi.nl/~aeb/math/dsrg/dsrg.html">Parameters of directed strongly regular graphs</a>.
%H A399766 L. K. Jørgensen, <a href="https://vbn.aau.dk/da/publications/search-for-directed-strongly-regular-graphs">Search for directed strongly regular graphs</a>, Research Report Series R-99-2016, Aalborg University (1999).
%e A399766 For n = 15, the complementary parameter classes (15,4,2,1,1) and (15,10,8,6,7) have 5 nonisomorphic graphs each, while (15,5,2,1,2) and (15,9,6,5,6) have 1292 each; hence a(15) = 2*5 + 2*1292 = 2594.
%Y A399766 Cf. A076435, A088741.
%K A399766 nonn,more,new
